		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4757&amp;p=35129#p35129"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>@VK3KYY<br>Thanks for your answer, I have a lot of DMR transceivers in use and they are all displayed in the CPS in the ID list, which is also useful for editing a contact manually. Why doesn't that work in the Opengd77 CPS for the MD2017? Unfortunately, only the call sign is displayed in the transceiver, even with the setting 2 lines and 50??</div></blockquote>It does display the full contact if the DMR ID database is successfuly loaded. Also, the lookup order matters (see <a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#order" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... e.md#order</a>).<br><br>The codeplug itself supports only 1024 contact, with a 16 characters limit, that's why the DMR ID database is located elsewhere in the device flash memory, and not available in the CPS.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Mon Jan 13, 2025 7:07 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
